{"name":"Meatloaf","hex":"#663311","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meatloaf","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dish of ground meat (usually made from ground beef, although lamb, pork, veal, venison, poultry and seafood are also used) formed into a loaf shape, mixed with egg and breadcrumbs, then baked or smoked, and usually served in slices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meatloaf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meatloaf","blocks":[{"text":"Meatloaf is a dish of ground meat combined with other ingredients, formed into the shape of a loaf, then baked or smoked. It may be hand-formed on a baking tray or pan-formed in a loaf pan. It is usually made with ground beef, although ground lamb, pork, veal, venison, poultry, and seafood are also used, sometimes in combination. Vegetarian adaptations of meatloaf may use imitation meat or pulses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/MeatloafWithSauce.jpg/330px-MeatloafWithSauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meatloaf","wikidata":"Q3807565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sekan%C3%A1_007.jpg/500px-Sekan%C3%A1_007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sekan%C3%A1_007.jpg/1280px-Sekan%C3%A1_007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sekan%C3%A1_007.jpg/500px-Sekan%C3%A1_007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Czech sekaná","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASekan%C3%A1_007.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Homemade_Pork_Embutido.jpg/500px-Homemade_Pork_Embutido.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x